A||N||2||fierose||Belt Change 2.5 SE w/ac||||1||
Z||000000||fierose||05-24-2000||04:04 AM||||I know this seems like a pretty easy feat.  But all I want to do is change the belts on 85 2.5L fiero w/ac.  I can take the alternator belt off fine but when I go to take off the compressor belt I can't find a mount with a pivot on it to loosen the belt.  I've looked all over in the haynes manual and searched the archives here I really must not be seeing something because I looked everywhere on the car.  I'm pretty sure they didn't put a belt tensioner on the earlier models but I'm not sure.  If you know where I need to loosen on the mount please be specific because I'm not finding it.  <P>Thanks<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Brian84SE||05-24-2000||07:29 AM||||You must loosen the air cond. compressor.  I did it from underneath. Jack up the car and support it with jackstands.  It also helps to remove the right rear wheel.  You may not be able to see things up there all that well.  I felt around until I found it. If memory serves me correctly, there was a foward and rear bolt that I loosened.||||reg||1
Z||000002||deceler8||05-24-2000||09:21 AM||||Loosening the A/C compressor is easy...tightening it is isn't. I recommend you check out a fanbelt tightener...available through JC Whitney and possibly your local auto parts store. Last saw them in Harbor Freight for $2.99.<P>The amount of pulling, pushing and swearing this tool saves is amazing. Trust me.||||reg||1
